WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.150
- The votes for President
of the United States

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.970
are as follows.

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.450
Joseph R. Biden Junior
of the State of Delaware

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.100
has received 306 votes.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.510
Donald J. Trump of the State of Florida

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.940
has received 232 votes.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.950
(crowd shouting)

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.960
- [Narrator] After a nearly
four-hour violent standoff

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.428
inside the nation's Capitol,

00:00:20.428 --> 00:00:22.310
(gavel banging)
(Congress clapping)

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.590
Congress reconvened
Wednesday night to certify

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.720
Democratic President Elect Joe
Biden's Electoral College win

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.040
in the November election.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.000
- We know that we would be part of history

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.090
in a positive way today.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.090
Every four years when we demonstrate again

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.370
the peaceful transfer of power

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.913
from one president to the next.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.020
And despite the shameful actions of today,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.030
we feel we'll do so.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.570
- And I've traveled the world with Joe.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:55.823
I hope he lost, I prayed
he would lose, he won.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.312
He's the legitimate president
of the United States.

00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:01.698
(glass banging)

00:01:01.698 --> 00:01:03.500
- [Man] They're breaking the window.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.480
- [Man] Get in, get in.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.250
- [Narrator] Later that
day, around 2 p.m.,

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.270
pro-Trump rioters jumped barricades

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.670
and smashed windows, quickly
overwhelming the police

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.917
and storming the Capitol building.

00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.499
- [Crowd] Stop the steal, stop the steal.

00:01:16.499 --> 00:01:19.499
- [Chuck] We'll stand in recess
until the call of the chair.

00:01:20.877 --> 00:01:22.280
- Protestors are in the building.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.113
- Thank you.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.910
- [Narrator] Lawmakers were interrupted,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.695
evacuated and ordered to lock
themselves in their offices

00:01:29.695 --> 00:01:32.432
as hundreds of rioters
entered the building.

00:01:32.432 --> 00:01:33.265
- Yeah.

00:01:35.985 --> 00:01:37.870
- [Narrator] Some could be
seen throughout the building

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.840
waving Trump and American flags

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.080
and cheering from the balconies

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.598
as thousands of other people
surrounded the building.

00:01:43.598 --> 00:01:47.015
- [Crowd] Stop the steal. Stop the steal.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.200
- [Narrator] One of them
was shot by Capitol police

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.050
and three others starting the unrest.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.320
About an hour before
the violence broke out,

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.140
President Trump spoke to
supporters at a rally.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.120
- We're going to walk
down Pennsylvania Avenue,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.090
I love Pennsylvania Avenue,

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.870
and we're going to the Capitol.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:10.890
We're going to try and
give our Republicans,

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.440
the weak ones, because the
strong ones don't need any

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.640
of our help,

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.840
we're going to try and give them the kind

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.710
of pride and boldness that they need

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.304
to take back our country.

00:02:22.304 --> 00:02:25.360
- [Brett] At Trump's
speech in the morning,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.240
it seemed like a fairly contained,

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.009
fairly organized event.

00:02:30.009 --> 00:02:31.657
- [Crowd] USA.

00:02:31.657 --> 00:02:33.267
- Pull them this way.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:34.670
- [Brett] But at the Capitol,

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.420
things really changed.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.240
And it suddenly felt out of control.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.750
And you weren't sure which
way things were going,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.710
where the energy in the crowd was going.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.610
- [Man] Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.930
- [Narrator] President Elect Joe Biden

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:49.010
condemned the violence

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.500
and called for the certification

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.180
of the Electoral College
results to continue.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:55.160
- This is not dissent.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.980
It's disorder.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.960
It's chaos.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:00.533
It borders on sedition.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.603
And it must end now.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.040
I call on this mob

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.710
to pull back and allow
the work of democracy

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.010
to go forward.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.600
- [Narrator] Shortly after he spoke,

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.460
President Trump posted a
recorded video on social media.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.600
- It was a landslide election

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.130
and everyone knows it,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.570
especially the other side.

00:03:22.570 --> 00:03:24.600
But you have to go home now.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.290
We have to have peace.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.150
We have to have law and order.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.900
- [Narrator] The video was
later removed by Twitter,

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.610
YouTube and Facebook for
violating their policies.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.537
Facebook's VP of integrity said,

00:03:35.537 --> 00:03:37.370
"This is an emergency situation

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.220
and we removed it because on balance,

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:40.900
we believe it contributes to,

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.877
rather than diminishes the
risk of ongoing violence."

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.190
Trump later tweeted, "These are the things

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.250
and events that happen

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.200
when a sacred landslide election victory

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.580
is so unceremoniously

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.970
and viciously stripped away

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.110
from great patriots who have been badly

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:57.070
and unfairly treated for so long.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.730
Go home with love and in peace.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.780
Remember this day forever!"

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.860
Following that tweet,

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:04.270
Twitter locked the president's
account for 12 hours

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:05.730
and warned that further violations

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.480
could lead it to permanently suspend

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.680
the president's account.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.360
The violence at the
Capitol prompted District

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.090
of Columbia mayor, Muriel Bowser,

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.890
to declare a 6 p.m. curfew

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.430
and more than 1,000 D.C.
National Guard troops

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:20.310
were called in to help maintain order.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.150
1,000 New York National Guard members

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.210
will also be deployed.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.820
Some White House staffers resigned,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.230
following the events of the day,

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:29.730
including a top National
Security Council official

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.300
and the First Lady's Chief of Staff

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.563
and press secretary.

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.720
The scenes of violence drew condemnation

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.300
from leaders around the world.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.070
- What happened today in
Washington, D.C. is not America.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:41.903
Definitely.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.723
We believe in the strength
of our democracies.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.920
- [Narrator] As rioters
broke into the Capitol

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.560
around 2 p.m. Wednesday,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.700
lawmakers had just begun
discussing a challenge

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.200
by some Republican lawmakers

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:58.950
to the vote tally in Arizona,

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:01.700
a debate that exposed a deep
divide within the party.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:05.160
- What does it say to the
nearly half the country

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.230
that believes this election was rigged

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:11.710
if we vote not even to consider the claims

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.213
of illegality and fraud in this election?

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.840
And I believe there's a better way.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.540
- If this election were overturned

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.193
by mere allegations from the losing side,

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.613
our democracy would enter a disbar.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:36.863
We'd never see the whole nation
accept an election again.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:39.750
- [Narrator] When Congress reconvened,

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.880
the day of unrest
prompted some Republicans

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:43.380
to reconsider their decision

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.660
to object to the certification of votes.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.100
- Following the events of today,

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:49.560
it appears that some signatures

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.740
have withdrawn their objection.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:54.680
(Congress clapping)

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.580
- When I arrived in
Washington this morning,

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.100
I fully intended to object

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:00.296
to the certification of electoral votes.

00:06:00.296 --> 00:06:03.170
However, the events that
have transpired today

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.336
have forced me to reconsider

00:06:04.336 --> 00:06:07.310
and I cannot now in good conscience object

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:08.630
to the certification

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.963
of these electors.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:13.170
- [Narrator] But some Republicans stood

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.810
by their decision to object.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.140
- Because for those who have concerns

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.770
about the integrity of our elections,

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:20.750
those who have concerns about
what happened in November,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:23.100
this is the appropriate means.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.030
This is the lawful place

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.580
where those objections and
concerns should be heard.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.186
Not through violence,

00:06:30.186 --> 00:06:32.840
not by appealing from ballots to bullets

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.000
but here in this lawful process.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.050
- [Narrator] After Congress
certified Biden's victory,

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:39.570
President Trump issued a statement,

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.530
committing to an orderly
transition of power

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:45.152
on January 20th, despite
disagreeing with the outcome.

00:06:45.152 --> 00:06:47.902
(dramatic music)

